main = draw v = Normal in if v == 1.0 then left () else right v
-- Every sample with v /= 1 returns Right v, so the payload's density at 1.0
-- is the Normal's (0.2420, dim 1) -- the value on every neighbourhood of 1.
-- The set-witness engine removes the point 1 from the whole line for the
-- False arm, and the query point 1.0 meets that removal as a disequality:
-- impossible. A point removed from an interval's bound already closes back
-- (set-witness/setWitnessNegatedComparisonBoundary); a point removed from the
-- whole line or an interval's inside stays removed, because the engine cannot
-- tell a query point from the event point of a second `v == 1.0`
-- (set-witness/setWitnessContinuousEqualsTwice pins that one as empty).
-- Verified on dev at the fix of null-set-conventions-not-preserved-under-negation,
-- interpreter. Docs task set-witness-null-set-boundary-conventions.
